# dbt Labs

> dbt is the standard for data transformation, letting data teams work
> like software engineers. dbt Labs builds dbt Core, dbt Fusion and the
> dbt platform, used by tens of thousands of teams to build, test and
> document analytics code.

Every page listed below is available as markdown: the `.md` URL returns
the markdown version, and removing `.md` gives the standard page. Any of
these pages also responds to an `Accept: text/markdown` request header.

Full text of all content: https://www.getdbt.com/llms-full.txt
By section: /llms-full-pages.txt, /llms-full-blog.txt, /llms-full-case-studies.txt, /llms-full-resources.txt, /llms-full-events.txt, /llms-full-dbt-summit.txt

Working with a limited context window? https://www.getdbt.com/llms-full-blog-recent.txt
has the 50 most recent blog posts in full and is small
enough to load in one request; the complete blog file is not.

In the llms-full files, documents are separated by a line containing only
`---`, and each document opens with a YAML frontmatter block giving its
title and canonical url. Thematic breaks within a document use `***`, so a
line of `---` always marks a document or frontmatter boundary and never
appears inside a document body.

