## Blog

- [Why your AI pilot stalled at the context gap](https://www.getdbt.com/blog/why-your-ai-pilot-stalled-at-the-context-gap.md): Many AI projects are stuck. Don’t blame the models. The problem is a lack of trusted context. Here’s how you solve it.
- [Scaling AI is easy. Trusting it is hard.](https://www.getdbt.com/blog/scaling-ai-is-easy-trusting-it-is-hard.md): As AI scales, cracks in data trust and governance start to show. Here's what breaks first, and what it takes to fix it.
- [Databricks processes your data. dbt defines what it means](https://www.getdbt.com/blog/databricks-processes-your-data-dbt-defines-what-it-means.md): Your compute platform and your transformation logic are two separate decisions. Most executives approve them as one.
- [dbt Core v1.12 is GA](https://www.getdbt.com/blog/dbt-core-v1-12-is-ga.md): dbt Core v1.12: what's new and how to upgrade.
- [Model for the token, not the table](https://www.getdbt.com/blog/model-for-the-token-not-the-table.md): We were burning through Gong's API to feed AI. Modeling the transcripts in the warehouse with dbt cut token costs 20x.
- [Why agentic projects fail and how to fix them](https://www.getdbt.com/blog/why-agentics-projects-fail-and-how-to-fix-them.md): Why do some AI deployments yield great successes while so many still crash and burn? The answer is in the data.
- [How dbt State cuts warehouse compute and speeds up every run](https://www.getdbt.com/blog/dbt-state-use-case.md): How Fanatics cut warehouse compute by only rebuilding what's changed
- [dbt Summit 2026: the keynotes and product sessions](https://www.getdbt.com/blog/dbt-summit-2026-keynotes-product-sessions.md): The dbt Summit 2026 keynotes and the product sessions behind them.
